{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Breached Credential Detected",
	"Description": "Okta matched a password used at sign-in against a known breached credential corpus. The password is public, so treat the account as needing a reset even if the sign-in itself succeeded and looked normal.\n\nEvent type: security.breached_credential.detected\n\nReference(s):\n- https://help.okta.com/en-us/content/topics/security/password-health-report.htm\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
